{"title":"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5_(answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5 (answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Pythagorean_Triples)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Pythagorean Triples)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c3969a7b74a9d8c09fbc85c40ec7411e8f77ae6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{2} + 4^{2} + 12^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2551d599d67ef522af7a46aa54f63f293a30e621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 13^{2} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 19^{2} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 17^{2} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 15^{2} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 11^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"471\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/14833fa77c0b86ac9068d2edcfa675e2a4d77b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2 + 4^2 + 12^{2} = 9 + 16 + 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66aebf6189de139226782e2e5d3bcf58f3358b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=25 + 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f8a900a506a8e21549fd011ed879864fbefae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f0987e55a8830107ba990d82317f276b9005866c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 13^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"94\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.5_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5_(answer_choices)\">Solution 1.5 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we didn't know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8bef5bd5e97964bd8c2fcce4f841c0b6460583f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^{2} = 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> in solution 1, we could have realized that the units digit of the square of the number wanted must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3629b1f1f3b22f1a3c927c7ac0467574394f17ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This only occurs when the number being squared has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, eliminating answer all answer choices except A and C. We can then try one of these, and then choose the other if we get a different answer from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3629b1f1f3b22f1a3c927c7ac0467574394f17ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>We can then see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/2/9029ac95ea8278fa97392332f0501525b0d77e7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\times 13 = 13 \\times 10 + 13 \\times 3 = 130 + 39 = 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"358\" height=\"15\" />, which is exactly what we want. This means that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f0987e55a8830107ba990d82317f276b9005866c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 13^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"94\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>We could have also realized that the square root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f626ff046119cbaaa87c0c5df3f1203b9a28347f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23edbf52de8a888576be3c91a8738bc8ada924ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2} &gt; 1.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5f5a794d8b7b74e970990b59968b1321e5c267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\sqrt{2} &gt; 10 \\times 1.4 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" />, meaning that the answer would have to be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/3759b815e56fbb5bd6e0ea2458b1a18512b100d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169 &lt; 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Pythagorean_Triples.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Pythagorean_Triples)\">Solution 2 (Pythagorean Triples)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Pythagorean Triples)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> form a pythagorean triple, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/0791ed7d498e0000abf5cadf8e3617d0e7fb2036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{2} + 4^{2} = 5^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/2995707b4e1a151a1898044e2b01801e9b3eb0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{2} + 4^{2} + 12^{2} = 5^{2} + 12^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Next, we realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> form a pythagorean triple, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f6488bc0ca9deefa3bdc8be69efc2316977cfa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2} + 12^{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 13^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Lgnjqr28Lnk?si=IMxJfX4CiM0ZVN1z&amp;t=99\">https://youtu.be/Lgnjqr28Lnk?si=IMxJfX4CiM0ZVN1z&amp;t=99</a> (also includes problems 1-4 and 6-10)\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley\">2009 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</